s. </>",
    ["Even if he did guess... he's so timid, he definitely wouldn't dare come looking, hee hee."] = "I'm playing hide-and-seek with Billy! He'd never guess I could run this far while he counted to one hundred.",
    ["Every cosmetic has a base Fashion Value. Players can consume dyeing materials to dye and save schemes to obtain additional Fashion Value bonuses. Each <Highlight>1</> Coral Dye consumed in a scheme grants <Highlight>10</> Fashion Value, each <Highlight>1</> Rainbow Dye grants <Highlight>40</> Fashion Value, each <Highlight>1</> Foam Dye grants <Highlight>20</> Fashion Value, and each Divine Favor Card consumed grants <Highlight>4000</> Fashion Value. The system will select the <Highlight> 3 </> schemes with the highest additional Fashion Value from all saved dyeing schemes for this cosmetic and add them to the base Fashion Value as the final Fashion Value of the cosmetic. \n\nExample: \nThe base Fashion Value of a certain cosmetic equipment is <Highlight>800</>. The player has saved <Highlight>4 </> dyeing schemes for this cosmetic, and the additional Fashion Value provided by the four schemes are <Highlight>150, 280, 420, 360</>. \nThe system will select the <Highlight> 3 </> schemes with the highest additional Fashion Value from these <Highlight> 4 </> schemes (i.e., 420, 360, 280) for settlement; the remaining schemes will not participate in the calculation. \nTherefore, the cumulative dyeing bonus for this cosmetic is 420 + 360 + 280 = 1060, and the final total Fashion Value is the base Fashion Value of 800 plus the cumulative dyeing bonus of 1060, which is 1860. \n\nSupplementary Notes: \n1. After adding or modifying a dyeing scheme, the system will automatically select the highest <Highlight> 3 </> schemes to participate in the settlement and update the Fashion Value of this cosmetic. \n2. Deleting a dyeing scheme will simultaneously remove it from the settlement queue. If the deleted scheme was originally participating in the settlement, it will be replaced by the next highest remaining scheme. \n3. If the player has not saved any dyeing schemes, the cosmetic will only display the base Fashion Value."] = "Every cosmetic has a base Fashion Value. Players can consume dyeing materials to dye and save schemes to obtain additional Fashion Value bonuses. Each <Highlight>1</> Coral Dye consumed in a scheme grants <Highlight>10</> Fashion Value, each <Highlight>1</> Rainbow Dye grants <Highlight>40</> Fashion Value, each <Highlight>1</> Foam Dye grants <Highlight>20</> Fashion Value, and each Divine Favor Card consumed grants <Highlight>4000</> Fashion Value. The system will select the <Highlight> 3 </> schemes with the highest additional Fashion Values from all saved dyeing schemes for this cosmetic and add them to the base Fashion Value to determine the cosmetic's final Fashion Value. \n\nExample: \nThe base Fashion Value of a certain cosmetic item is <Highlight>800</>. The player has saved <Highlight>4 </> dyeing schemes for this cosmetic, and the additional Fashion Values provided by the four schemes are <Highlight>150, 280, 420, 360</>. \nThe system will select the <Highlight> 3 </> schemes with the highest additional Fashion Values from these <Highlight> 4 </> schemes (i.e., 420, 360, 280) for calculation; the remaining schemes will not be included. \nTherefore, the cumulative dyeing bonus for this cosmetic is 420 + 360 + 280 = 1060, and the final total Fashion Value is the base Fashion Value of 800 plus the cumulative dyeing bonus of 1060, which is 1860. \n\nSupplementary Notes: \n1. After adding or modifying a dyeing scheme, the system will automatically select the highest <Highlight> 3 </> schemes for the calculation and update the Fashion Value of this cosmetic. \n2. Deleting a dyeing scheme will also remove it from the calculation. If the deleted scheme was originally included, it will be replaced by the next-highest remaining scheme. \n3. If the player has not saved any dyeing schemes, the cosmetic will display only its base Fashion Value.",
    ["Everything in the world is but a play; you and I are both actors, no need to be so serious."] = "Everything in the world is but a play; you and I are both actors in it, so there is no need to be so serious.",
    ["Finally about to finish. There's one last step. Miss Justice, should I send he to Tingen now?"] = "Almost finished. There's just one last step. Miss Justice, should I send him to Tingen now?",
    ["Find a summon created by self (put into blackboard)."] = "Find a summon created by the player (store it on the blackboard).",
    ["Find the location of a summon created by self (put into blackboard)."] = "Find the location of a summon created by the player (store it on the blackboard).",
    ["Forget it, I'll ask Bessie in a while... She's a bit Silence today, who made her angry?"] = "Forget it, I'll ask Bessie in a while... She's a bit quiet today. Who made her angry?",
    ["Forget it, whose ancestors weren't glorious? Now, you're your jeweler, and I'm my dock worker..."] = "Oh, please. Whose ancestors weren't once prosperous? Now you're a jeweler, and I'm a dockworker...",
    ["Fortunately, they have also responded to my love one after another."] = "Fortunately, they responded to my affection one after another.",
    ["Gameplay not yet open."] = "Gameplay is not yet available.",
    ["Gift of the Earth: Filter 10 allies with lowest HP"] = "Gift of the Earth: Select the 10 allies with the lowest HP.",
    ["Going out to buy groceries every day and chatting with you is when I am happiest."] = "Going out to buy groceries and chatting with you every day are the happiest parts of my day.",
    ["Good afternoon, meeting you is truly an unexpected joy. Would you be willing to join me for afternoon tea on the way?"] = "Good afternoon. Meeting you is a delightful surprise. Would you care to join me for afternoon tea while you're here?",
    ["Hahaha, what you said is a fact. As you can see, I'm not good at tending to gardens, I just don't want Mr. Neil's garden to be abandoned like this."] = "Hahaha, what you said is true. As you can see, I'm not good at tending a garden; I just don't want Mr. Neil's garden to fall into ruin.",
    ["Hee hee, Cecil, stop teasing me! The way you look so serious... it really makes it hard to tell if it's a joke or real."] = "No, Edith. This power is wondrous, but dangerous too. Knowing too much won't do you any good; it's enough for me to protect you.",
    ["Heh, I'm afraid even the youngest doesn't know this himself."] = "Of the four brothers, the eldest is mentally unwell and the second is physically frail, but Father has never treated them harshly. The youngest, Finian, is Father's illegitimate son by another woman, though Father publicly claimed that he was adopted from the slums.",
    ["Hmm, wuu wuu. <P_Heart>(I've decided, please let me join you.)</>"] = "Roar? <P_Heart>(Oh? You're back.)</>",
    ["Hmph, with the master's ability, making some new tea to fool those old stubborn people is not difficult at all! So inflexible!"] = "Enough, meow. The master left home precisely because he hates those teas used for fighting, meow.",
    ["Holding this weapon will give you the power of wind and electricity. Movement speed and Basic Attack Attack Speed are increased; when a Basic Attack hits, there is a probability of striking the target with lightning, causing damage and Stagnation. But if you are not careful, the lightning will also strike yourself."] = "Holding this weapon will grant you the power of wind and lightning. Movement Speed and Basic Attack Speed are increased; when a Basic Attack hits, there is a chance of striking the target with lightning, dealing damage and inflicting Stagnation. But if you are not careful, the lightning may strike you as well.",
    ["How to Aiming Shot"] = "How to Aim and Shoot",
    ["I am going to lose. But I still believe that numbers are far more profound and fascinating than words. \n\nMonte disagrees. So we each opened a secret book, risking death or becoming a puppet, to find proof from these two Sealed Artifacts. \n\nWhoever reads this by misfortune—you might share the same fate as me. This book devours numbers and information. And <InvHighlight>the three crystal balls are the only way to seal it again </>. Three, the smallest closed structure in geometry. After the numbers themselves are hidden, all you can rely on is the relationship between the numbers; this is your only hope. \n\nPlease remember: <InvHighlight>α equals the number of characters in the title of the \"Book of Disorder\" </>, it is the first number that contains a relationship, and all numbers before it are indivisible wholes. \n\n<InvHighlight> α</> equals <InvHighlight>4</> \n<InvHighlight> β</> equals <InvHighlight>3</> \n<InvHighlight> ω</> equals <InvHighlight>2</> "] = "I am going to lose. But I still believe that numbers are far more profound and fascinating than words. \n\nMonte disagrees. So we each opened a secret book, risking death or becoming a puppet, to find proof from these two Sealed Artifacts. \n\nWhoever reads this by misfortune—you might share the same fate as me. This book devours numbers and information. And <InvHighlight>the three crystal balls are the only way to seal it again </>. Three, the smallest closed structure in geometry. After the numbers themselves are hidden, all you can rely on is the relationship between the numbers; this is your only hope. \n\nPlease remember: <InvHighlight>α equals the number of characters in the title of the \"Book of Disorder\" </>. It is the first number that contains a relationship, and all numbers before it are indivisible wholes. \n\n<InvHighlight> α</> equals <InvHighlight>4</> \n<InvHighlight> β</> equals <InvHighlight>3</> \n<InvHighlight> ω</> equals <InvHighlight>2</> ",
    ["I can no longer see any humanity in you. The you from the past would at least occasionally make me feel warmth, but the you now is a true monster."] = "I can no longer see any humanity in you. Your past self would at least occasionally make me feel warmth, but who you are now is a true monster.",
    ["I don't know either... why did it have to be given to Ray Bieber?"] = "I don't know either... Why does the notebook have to be given to Ray Bieber?",
    ["I finally found it... why did it have to coincide with Mr. Alger's return, sigh..."] = "I finally found it... Why did Mr. Alger have to come back just now? Sigh...",
    ["I plan to make a classic sign, da-da-da-da! \"The wind that misses you has blown to the Tarot Club\", how about that?"] = "I'm planning to make a classic sign. Ta-da! ‘The wind that misses you has blown all the way to the Tarot Club.’ What do you think?",
    ["I stood at the bow of the \"Black Throne,\" spread my arms, and said to Green and Edwards and the others: \"Do you want my treasure? Then go to the end of the Fog Sea to find it; I have hidden all my treasures there!\" \n But they didn't understand my humor at all and actually asked me if there was really any extra treasure. How boring; you guys can't be my Four Knights of the Apocalypse like this! But they were still willing to follow me on adventures in that sea full of fog. \n I have been thinking, to the west of the Northern Continent is the Fog Sea, and to the east is the Sonia Sea. I suspect that there are other continents at the ends of these two great oceans, just like the Southern Continent is at the end of the Berserk Sea. Maybe I can discover a brand new continent, the Western Continent! \n Set sail, great navigator Roselle Columbus Magellan Gustav, go and verify your conjecture!"] = "I stood at the bow of the \"Black Throne,\" spread my arms, and said to Green, Edwards, and the others: \"Do you want my treasure? Then go to the end of the Fog Sea to find it; I have hidden all my treasure there!\" \n But they didn't understand my humor at all and actually asked me if there really was any extra treasure. How boring; you guys can't be my Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse like this! But they were still willing to follow me on adventures across that fog-shrouded sea. \n I have been thinking: to the west of the Northern Continent is the Fog Sea, and to the east is the Sonia Sea. I suspect that there are other continents at the ends of these two great oceans, just as the Southern Continent lies at the end of the Berserk Sea. Maybe I can discover a brand-new continent—the Western Continent! \n Set sail, great navigator Roselle Columbus Magellan Gustav, and verify your conjecture!",
    ["I told him this tavern was built brick by brick by us, you built the counter with your own hands, and I painted the walls myself."] = "That merchant in the overcoat offered three hundred gold pounds right away. He said he wanted to turn this place into a fashionable café.",
    ["I'm planning to make a classic sign, da-da-da-da! 'The wind that misses you has finally blown to the Tarot Club', how about that?"] = "I'm planning to make a classic sign. Ta-da! ‘The wind that misses you has finally blown all the way to the Tarot Club.’ What do you think?",
    ["If 0, it only causes a one-time damage."] = "If set to 0, it deals damage only once.",
    ["If I hear that terrible excuse 'my cat is lying on the typewriter and won't let me write' again, I really won't be able to help sending a telegram to the editor to report all her past excuses for missing deadlines."] = "If I hear that terrible excuse 'my cat is lying on the typewriter and won't let me write' again, I really won't be able to help but send a telegram to the editor reporting all her past excuses for missing deadlines.",
    ["If it were only you, could you still hold up? I think that even if Eric hit you one more time, you would fall to the ground."] = "If you were alone, could you still hold out? I think one more punch from Eric would knock you to the ground.",
    ["If you have the ability, move out! Being with you is really bad luck!"] = "Move out if you dare! Being around you brings nothing but bad luck!",
    ["If you have the ability, then move out! Being with you is really bad luck!"] = "Move out if you dare! Being around you brings nothing but bad luck!",
    ["In the mad Extraordinary World, only the promise to you is my eternal anchor."] = "In the madness of the Beyonder world, my promise to you is my only eternal anchor.",
    ["Increases Armor Break by 250. When releasing a Finisher Skill, Armor Break is increased by an additional 250, and a heal is dealt at the target's location, with a maximum of 1 trigger every 12 seconds."] = "Increases Armor Break by 250. When using a Finisher Skill, Armor Break is increased by an additional 250, and a healing effect is created at the target's location. This can trigger at most once every 12 seconds.",
    ["Inviting people to taste delicious food is never a trouble! And true delicacies have a \"flowering period,\" it is my honor to let more people taste them within that period."] = "Inviting people to enjoy good food is never a bother! Besides, true delicacies have a limited season, and it is my honor to let more people enjoy them while they are at their best.",
    ["Is it being used \n Used by Warrior and other class sides."] = "Is it in use? \n Used by classes such as Warrior.",
    ["Is this fact or legend! It's written so brilliantly! It would be great if it were published as a standalone book."] = "I don't care about any of that. Look here—the serialized Tales of the Water-Lily Fairy!",
    ["Jeremy is not my brother anymore... wuu wuu..."] = "If you keep making that long face, I'll put wormwood in your dinner!",
    ["Just now after I finished grocery shopping, a little one said he would help me carry the bag for only 1 pence. Are children nowadays all this clever?"] = "Just after I finished grocery shopping, a little fellow offered to carry my bag for only 1 penny. Are children these days all so clever?",
    ["La la la la la—cough cough! Cough cough!"] = "Hey, I'm going to become the best guitarist in Ramde! I'm offering you this luck—do you want it or not?",
    ["Let's start with the first small test. The dock worker Brady has disappeared. This is the evidence left at the scene; remember to check it carefully."] = "Let's begin with a little test. The dockworker Brady has disappeared. This evidence was left at the scene, so remember to examine it carefully.",
    ["Look at me, 8 pennies is enough for me!"] = "Look at me, 8 pence is enough for me!",
    ["Look at these golden and translucent fried eggs, slightly charred at the edges, runny inside, simple but full of the taste of home, one bite will make you feel warm and satisfied, buy five get one free!"] = "Look at these golden, translucent fried eggs: slightly charred at the edges, runny inside, simple yet full of the taste of home. One bite will make you feel warm and satisfied. Buy five, get one free!",
    ["Margaret, seeing you again, Pete and I are both very happy, really."] = "Margaret, Pete and I are truly happy to see you again. We really are.",
    ["May 23rd\n　　Neil said he has walked this path seven times.\n　　He said it three times along the way, but I don't believe it—if he really had walked it seven times, why wouldn't he even know how to set up a tent? I crouched behind him, watching him put the tent fabric on backward for the third time. Snow water seeped into my gloves, cold as if it were licking my bones.\n　　Fortunately, we set up the tent before dark.\n\nRemaining supplies:\nBread: 6 portions (Peggy prepared 18 lbs for us, divided into 8 portions)\nDried meat and sausages: 5 portions\nSugar: 1 jar\nButter: 4 blocks\nWine: 3 bottles (Wine: 3 bottles → 2 bottles (1 consumed for the evening celebration))\nWater: 5 bottles (Temporarily sufficient; can keep an eye out for water sources on the way)"] = "May 23rd\n　　Neil said he had traveled this path seven times.\n　　He said it three times along the way, but I don't believe it—if he really had walked it seven times, why wouldn't he even know how to set up a tent? I crouched behind him, watching him put the tent fabric on backward for the third time. Snow water seeped into my gloves, cold as if it were licking my bones.\n　　Fortunately, we set up the tent before dark.\n\nRemaining supplies:\nBread: 6 portions (Peggy prepared 18 lbs for us, divided into 8 portions)\nDried meat and sausages: 5 portions\nSugar: 1 jar\nButter: 4 blocks\nWine: 3 bottles (Wine: 3 bottles → 2 bottles (1 consumed for the evening celebration))\nWater: 5 bottles (Temporarily sufficient; can keep an eye out for water sources on the way)",
    ["My Goddess, you saying this really saved this street. {{PlayerName}}, do you have any way to avoid a head-on confrontation?"] = "My Goddess, what you said may have just saved this entire street. {{PlayerName}}, do you have any way to avoid a head-on confrontation?",
    ["Neatly Written Writing Board"] = "Writing Board with Neat Handwriting",
    ["No, Edith, this power is magical, but also dangerous. Knowing too much is not good for you; having me to protect you is enough."] = "Really? How could you not teach me something so amazing?",
    ["Ooga, lost, I, dance steps, can't keep up, woo woo"] = "Ooga, big talk! Then let's have a dance-off! The loser eats rotten bananas! Ooga!",
    ["Or maybe forget it, our factory has gone on strike so many times, and I've never seen it have any real effect."] = "Or maybe we should forget it. We've gone on strike so many times at our factory, and not once has it actually worked.",
    ["Panic and flee! It's all a futile struggle! The only thing waiting for you is being swallowed by the living corpses!"] = "Flee in terror! All your struggles are futile! All that awaits you is being devoured by the living corpses!",
    ["Participate in the Club Brawl challenge, highest proportion of AOE damage received."] = "In Club Brawl, have the highest proportion of AOE damage taken.",
    ["Participate in the Club Brawl challenge, lowest total average of three statistics."] = "In Club Brawl, have the lowest overall average across all three statistics.",
    ["Participate in the Club Brawl challenge, shortest total survival time."] = "In Club Brawl, have the shortest total survival time.",
    ["Raphael, as the younger brother of the Viscountess, died on the night of the family's destruction years ago. \n He was a strong child in his lifetime, proud of his fists and strength, and was his sister's loyal follower and Guardian. \n After he was reborn under the gaze of the Great Mother, he became even more powerful and fierce, at the cost of losing human intelligence and forgetting everything from his past life—except for one thing: he had to guard someone. \n Who was it... where... the person to protect... must not forget... \n \"Stay here well and complete the guardianship of the offspring.\" After many years had passed, a voice said to him. \n Raphael leaned against the giant cocoon, feeling a special throb, as if it were a call from his bloodline, waking him from his stupor. He instinctively opened his mouth to call out a word buried deep in his memory: Sister... Sister... \n I finally found you... Sister... \n The light of the crimson ring flashed by. \n He had never forgotten the promise of his childhood. \n Even if he had become a terrifying sight, he would surely use all his strength to guard everything he cherished."] = "Raphael, the Viscountess's younger brother, died on the night his family was destroyed years ago. \n He had been a strong child, proud of his fists and strength, and a loyal follower and protector of his sister. \n After being reborn under the gaze of the Great Mother, he became even stronger and fiercer, but at the cost of his human intelligence. He could remember nothing from his former life except one thing: he had to protect someone. \n Who was it... Where were they... The person he had to protect... He must not forget... \n \"Stay here and fulfill your duty to protect the offspring.\" At some point in the long years that followed, a voice spoke to him. \n Leaning beneath the giant cocoon, Raphael felt a peculiar throbbing, like a call from his own bloodline, rousing him from his stupor. Instinctively, he opened his mouth and called out a word buried deep in his memory: Sister... Sister... \n I finally found you... Sister... \n The crimson ring flashed. \n He had never forgotten his childhood promise. \n Even in this terrifying form, he would give everything he had to protect all that he treasured.",
    ["Reach level 47 \n, complete the story event 【Act IV · Homicide】 \n, and complete the story event 【Act V · Rat Hole】"] = "Reach level 47\nComplete the story event 【Act IV · Homicide】\nComplete the story event 【Act V · Rat Hole】",
    ["Reach level 51 \n, complete the story event 【Act V · Rat Hole】 \n, and complete the challenge event 【Hard · Face-Peeler】"] = "Reach level 51\nComplete the story event 【Act V · Rat Hole】\nComplete the challenge event 【Hard · Face-Peeler】",
    ["Recommended to upgrade first"] = "It is recommended to upgrade this first.",
    ["Regardless of whether you have a name or not, I think I will remember you, cute Mao Mao Cao."] = "And now I have a new name of my own. I'm no longer a forgettable little cat!",
    ["Relax! By the way, speaking of matches, let me tell you a fresh rumor: I heard a dock worker named Lawis nearby just lost his little daughter."] = "Relax! By the way, speaking of matches, here's a fresh rumor: I heard that a nearby dockworker named Lawis just lost his young daughter.",
    ["Riddle and I are somewhat well-known creators of the Art School, and one day we will become very famous!"] = "Every Saturday and Sunday from 19:30 to 21:00, this buff is enhanced to 【Radiant Society Glory】: rolls for Charisma- and Intuition-based checks gain +3; participating in Order activities grants a combat-stat buff.",
    ["Roar roar! Roar roar!"] = "It seems to be sneaking a look at the others of its kind...",
    ["Roar roar, roar roar? <P_Heart>(So, are you ready?)</>"] = "Mm, whimper... <P_Heart>(I've decided. Please let me join you.)</>",
    ["Sasrir retreats from the battlefield and manipulates the destructive Chaos Sea water to converge. <Disable>After 30 seconds, it will impact the battlefield, destroying all living things.</>"] = "Sasrir retreats from the battlefield and gathers the destructive waters of the Chaos Sea. <Disable>After 30 seconds, they will sweep across the battlefield and destroy every living thing.</>",
    ["Sealed Artifact: Green Bloom (Filter teammate with lowest HP)"] = "Sealed Artifact: Crystal Eye (empty filter used by ClientCastSkill for bots)",
