    ["Will increased by %s"] = "Will increases by %s",
    ["Wuu wuu Dad... praise the Water Lily... please."] = "Wuu, wuu... Dad... praise the Water Lily... please.",
    ["Wuu wuu wuu, where are the people? Where did everyone go?"] = "Roar, roar? (So, are you ready?)",
    ["Wuu wuu... Mom said that once the wine in this shop is sold out, she'll let me go out and travel..."] = "No one has ever seen the owner of this shop, and no one knows when they restock the wine!",
    ["Wuu wuu... Okay, wuu wuu..."] = "You... um, don't be sad! The wine will sell out eventually!",
    ["You coming to see my performance won't get you photographed, right? This is your critical campaign period."] = "You won't be photographed coming to see my performance, will you? This is a critical period in your campaign.",
    ["You didn't miss it. The you from the past had already returned."] = "You didn't miss it. Your past self had already returned.",
    ["You fall into an endless cycle of nightmares, and after experiencing multiple deaths and the destruction of your will, you wake up in the forest again, but except for the pain in your chest and temples, you can't remember anything. After investigation, you follow the revelations on the parchment and find the three prophetic items, but accidentally intrude upon a sacrifice ritual to an evil god. Fortunately, Mr. Fool appears in time to graft power from future fate onto you, helping you resist the corruption remaining in your dream. You do not submit to the evil god, eventually awakening the Undying Power and defeating the \"Moon Corruption.\" With the help of Mr. Fool and the Tarot Club, the corruption on you is temporarily sealed, and you are about to wake up in reality."] = "You are trapped in an endless cycle of nightmares. After dying repeatedly and having your will worn down, you awaken in the forest once more, unable to remember anything beyond the pain in your chest and temples. Following the revelations on the parchment, you track down the three prophetic objects, only to stumble into a ritual offering sacrifices to an evil god. Fortunately, Mr. Fool appears in time and grafts power from your future fate onto you, helping you resist the corruption left behind in the dream. You refuse to submit to the evil god, eventually awakening the Undying Power and defeating the \"Moon Corruption.\" With the help of Mr. Fool and the Tarot Club, the corruption within you is temporarily sealed, and you are about to awaken in reality.",
    ["You have gained some fate perception of the Monster Pathway Sequence 7, Lucky One, Pierce increased by 40%. You can faintly glimpse the trajectory of the enemy's next move, hitting the target with precision as if it were fated."] = "You have gained part of the fate-perception ability of the Monster Pathway's Sequence 7, Lucky One, increasing Pierce by 40%. You can faintly glimpse your enemy's next move and strike your target with fated precision.",
    ["Your invitation has been accepted, and the historical projection of %s is traveling through time. Wait a moment; a stroll belonging only to the two of you is about to begin."] = "Your invitation has been accepted. The historical projection of %s is traveling through time. Please wait a moment; a private stroll for two is about to begin.",
    ["{{PlayerName}}, you really are a, genius."] = "{{PlayerName}}, you really are a—genius.",
    ["—In that world, no one sacrificed their life in the battle against Megose. The Cathedral subsequently gave the Nighthawks squad that guarded all of Tingen the opportunity to take up posts in Backlund, but Dunn and Frye both refused. \n\n      Daly returned from Backlund late at night; she brought a bottle of the wine that both Dunn and Frye loved, as was her custom. \n      \"So, you really refused the Cathedral's invitation?\" She leaned against the table, her gaze resting on Dunn's face. \n      Dunn looked up at her. The firelight flickered gently in his gray eyes. \n      \"You are more suited for that place than I am,\" he said, his voice calm and heavy. \"In Tingen, the people here know me, and I know every street, every window. I want to stay here and continue guarding it.\" \n      Frye silently poured himself a glass and raised it: \"Me too.\" \n      Daly was silent for a moment, then laughed softly: \"I knew you would say that.\" \n      She grabbed the bottle and filled her own glass. Three glasses clinked together in front of the fireplace with a crisp sound. \n      Outside the window, Tingen slept quietly under the watchful eyes of the sleepless Guardians."] = "—In that world, no one died in the battle against Megose. The Cathedral subsequently gave the Nighthawks squad that guarded all of Tingen the opportunity to take up posts in Backlund, but Dunn and Frye both refused. \n\n      Daly returned from Backlund late at night; she brought a bottle of the wine that both Dunn and Frye loved, as was her custom. \n      \"So, you really refused the Cathedral's invitation?\" She leaned against the table, her gaze resting on Dunn's face. \n      Dunn looked up at her. The firelight flickered gently in his gray eyes. \n      \"You are more suited for that place than I am,\" he said, his voice calm and heavy. \"In Tingen, the people here know me, and I know every street, every window. I want to stay here and continue guarding it.\" \n      Frye silently poured himself a glass and raised it: \"Me too.\" \n      Daly was silent for a moment, then laughed softly: \"I knew you would say that.\" \n      She grabbed the bottle and filled her own glass. Three glasses clinked together in front of the fireplace with a crisp sound. \n      Outside the window, Tingen slept quietly under the watchful eyes of the sleepless guardians.",
}
